\title{zkVMs}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    Everything above, wrapped around an instruction set so that a program rather than a circuit is
    the thing being proved. A zkVM decomposes into three layers — the ISA, the VM architecture, and
    the proving layer — and most design disagreements are about where to put work between them.
}

\p{
    This is the object the [verified zkEVM effort](dhsorens-0045) is ultimately aimed at. A machine
    semantics in Lean is the first half of the statement one wants to prove about a zkVM; [LC3 in
    Lean](dhsorens-0027) is that half at small scale.
}

